WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.800
In the Fed

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.035
investors trust.

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:04.037
even as its campaign
to raise interest rates

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.438
causes turmoil in the

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:08.041
stock, bond, currency
and commodity markets

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.542
and increases the odds of

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.377
a global recession.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.611
Bloomberg polled a group of

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.146
professional and retail investors,

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.414
asking them

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:17.884 position:64%
which central bank will succeed
in cooling inflation and getting the cost

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.319
of living under control.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.488
The US won handedly.

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:23.123
That may be because
the rest of the world

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:24.624
faces additional pressures.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.092
For the UK and Europe,

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.561
it's an energy shortage
sparked by war in Ukraine,

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:31.765
while China is still pursuing
its Covid Zero policy.

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:32.699
In other words,

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.300
the US is the cleanest dirty shirt

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.635
in the global laundry basket.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.704
So it follows that
survey respondents

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.072
also overwhelmingly picked

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.608
the US economy
as the relative winner,

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:44.244
seen emerging from
the global turmoil first,

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:46.046
along with
U.S. stocks and bonds.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.080
Now, looking ahead,

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.915
one unspoken downside risk

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:49.482
in a recovery

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:52.152
is a potential widening
in inequality.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:53.653
The stock market would rally,

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.221
boosting the portfolios
of the wealthy

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.757
while stagnating pay
and high rents

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.726
would squeeze
lower-income households.

